 :ordering-and-cut {:construction ["Prove isolated process ownership and full relevant subscription; receive successful ACK on the one serialized event connection; consume but never count initial tick." "Issue unpredictable distinct pre nonce; consume matching first=false event on that same stream. After consumption request GET_TREE; wait for fully parsed bounded response. Then issue distinct post nonce and consume matching first=false event on that same stream. Serialize parsing and preserve byte-stream sequence numbers, queue capacity, generation and monotonic timestamps; send reply and callback timing are never barriers." "Reject any relevant event from pre through post; pre-tick orders earlier generated events according to qualified installed source/docs. Retain exact stream indices, generation, nonces, request/reply sequencing, limits, drop counters, complete coverage proof and independently established X-operation completion and exclusion. Pre/post fences do not show that an earlier X request has been processed by i3. Ensure fixture changes are causally completed using independently justified X/i3 synchronization and observed conditions; if unavailable stop, never assume sleep or quiet means completion." "GET_TREE and oracle tree must be bounded between the same fences and under explicit operation exclusion; no other writer, self-generated unobserved mutations, queue loss or unqualified event classes. Compare only if both captures represent the same established state; two separately timed snapshots are not automatically atomic. Post-cut changes revoke live lease; evidence is freshness at that particular cut only."]
                    :delays "Inject delays at a controlled proxy/transport delivery point, retain server-generation witness separately from receive sequence. An event generated before pre but delivered after the tree or a within-cut event delayed beyond the tree must invalidate candidate; if delayed behind post contradicts the assumed intact FIFO, treat it as proxy reorder/loss and invalidate ordering qualification, not as native behavior. Test missing/wrong/initial/reused tick, ACK rejection, channel drop, overflow, timeout and continual churn; no guessed success."
                    :coverage "Enumerate event types and every supported field/operation; establish event coverage from exact source and controlled negative probes. No proof of absence from merely receiving ticks, a quiet interval, or callback order. Unknown message, oversized frame, unsupported path or lost counter revokes coverage."}
 :oracle {:independence "Separate module, separate native GET_TREE request and independently written traversal of nodes and floating_nodes; no reuse of collector reducer, mapping code, snapshot parser or normalizer. Share only immutable fixture identity assignments and frozen schema. Cross-check explicit unique workspace fixture map and owned XID/incarnation table; unknown/duplicate/unowned identities deny. Record sanitized bounded tree-derived subset, independently normalized oracle, admitted owner replay subset, and their identity map."
          :comparison "Compare exact set of [epoch XID incarnation workspace-UUID] at the same justified quiescent cut; verify hierarchy/floating/move/resize through separate fixture stimulus and native tree structural assertions, not by claiming geometry or full-tree equality from subset. Both trees bounded to declared node/window/frame caps; omit titles/classes and unrelated fields from retained artifacts. If raw trees required to independently audit normalization, retain only synthetic-owned sanitized bounded tree including necessary hierarchy and no personal content."
          :identity "Explicitly record X server epoch, owning process identity, window create/close and per-lifetime fresh UUID; a repeated XID after close requires a new incarnation. Cross-epoch same XID never shares identity. After uncertain reconnect invalidate old lifetime/target and allocate fresh incarnation even when same numeric XID survives; do not migrate historical memberships. Actual forced XID reuse may be infeasible: if not observed, retain it as missing native coverage and verify deterministic same/cross-epoch collision schedules in offline tests only, never claim native reuse."}
